 "title": "DS90LV011A: single 3.3 V LVDS line driver in SOT-23-5",
 "source": {
  "document": "SNLS140C",
  "revision": "SNLS140C, May 2002, revised April 2013",
  "pages": 14
 },
 "summary": "One LVDS transmitter: a single-ended LVTTL/LVCMOS input is turned into a 350 mV typical differential output that meets TIA/EIA-644-A. The output stage is a current-mode driver, so power dissipation stays low at high frequency and the short-circuit fault current is small; it runs above 400 Mbps (200 MHz). It works from one 3.0 V to 3.6 V supply over −40 °C to +85 °C, its outputs go high-impedance when the supply is off, and the SOT-23 part has the pinout of the SN65LVDS1. DS90LV012A is the matching single receiver.",
