 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Driver",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A logic high on TTL IN drives OUT+ above OUT−, a low drives OUT− above OUT+. The output is a switched current source that develops about 350 mV across the 100 Ω line termination, centred near 1.2 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Load",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The driver needs a resistive load across OUT+ and OUT− to meet its specified figures; the characteristics are given with RL = 100 Ω."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Power off",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "With VDD at 0 V the outputs are high-impedance: leakage into OUT± is ±10 µA max with 3.6 V or GND applied."
  },
  {
